# NestJS backend

Layers:
- Controllers: validate DTO (class-validator), call one service method, map response/status. No logic.
- Services: business logic and use cases only. No raw SQL or Mongo calls.
- Repositories: all DB access. Parameterized queries only.
- Providers are wired in modules (composition root). Never `new` a repository or client inside a service.

Errors:
- Throw typed domain errors (`JobNotFoundError`), map to HTTP in a global exception filter.
- Never leak stack traces or internal messages in responses.

Structure (one responsibility per file):
```
apps/api/src/<feature>/
  <feature>.module.ts
  <feature>.controller.ts
  <feature>.service.ts
  <feature>.repository.ts
  dto/
  <feature>.service.spec.ts
```

Config: `@nestjs/config` with a validated schema; fail fast on missing env vars.
